// This is a comment

// Every stmt is global by default

// string can contain references to variables and stmnt
// statments
// stmt:[]type [variable name] [string]
stmt:decision a1 "@fast-restaurant"
stmt:decision a2 "because of @a1 the website"
stmt:unknown u2 "should @fast-restaurant website"

// statments can also be declared this way. When typed this way as soon as you type a `"` the lsp will generate a unique id and make a generic stmt
"" df131 stmt

// later on the user can type : after stmnt the lsp will bring up the list of types
"" df131 stmt:decision

